            <div xml:id="d567">

                <pb facs="0986" n="890" xml:id="pg890"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">853.51/314: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dearing</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-01-22T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 22,
                                1926—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>3. Your 4, January 19, noon. This Government is gratified by the issuance of
                    Decree No. 11388 providing a credit for the repurchase of Tobacco Bonds.
                    However, it still requires a definite assurance from the Portuguese Government
                    that this credit will be applied to American-held bonds before it can take any
                    action in the sense desired by the Portuguese Government.</p>
                <p>Your suggestion that the Portuguese Government designate a bank in America or
                    Europe where bonds belonging to Americans may, within a certain period, be
                    presented and paid as to principal and arrears of interest and this fact be made
                    public would offer a solution satisfactory to this Government, providing that
                    adequate time is given for the presentation of the bonds, and you may so inform
                    the Portuguese Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
